  "reporter": "<div style=\"width: 1280px; height: 1000px; overflow: hidden; background: #fff; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; color: #2B2723; position: relative\">\n<div style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 34%; height: 6px; background: #A0522D\"></div>\n<div style=\"height: 72px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 0 56px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ECE8E2\"><span style=\"font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 24px\">Maya Okonkwo</span><span style=\"display: flex; gap: 28px; font-size: 15px; color: #5A534C\"><span>Weddings</span><span>Portraits</span><span style=\"color: #2B2723; font-weight: 600\">Journal</span><span>Contact</span></span></div>\n<div style=\"padding: 40px 64px 0\">\n<div style=\"display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: stretch; margin-bottom: 48px\">\n<div style=\"flex: 0 0 40%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 16px\">\n<div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #766D64\">Home › Journal › Planning › Golden-Hour Ceremony</div>\n<div style=\"font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 40px; line-height: 1.12\">How to Plan a Golden-Hour Ceremony</div>\n<div style=\"font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.4; color: #5A534C\">Timing a sunset ceremony is mostly math and a little luck.</div>\n<div style=\"height: 1px; background: #ECE8E2\"></div>\n<div style=\"font-size: 16px; color: #766D64\">Maya Okonkwo · Oct 2, 2026 · 6 min read</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex: 1; aspect-ratio: 3 / 2; background: #E9E5DF url(/template-photos/golden-hour-ceremony.webp) center / cover no-repeat; border-radius: 4px\"></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; gap: 36px; align-items: flex-start\">\n<div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px\">\n\n\n<p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.75; color: #3A342F\">Golden hour is the stretch of soft, low light just before sunset. It is short, it moves every week, and it is the thing couples ask me about most.</p>\n\n\n<p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.75; color: #3A342F\">The trick is to plan backwards. Look up the sunset time for your date and location, then count back about an hour. That is roughly when the light turns warm and directional, and it is when you want to be finishing your vows, not starting them.</p>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin: 8px 0 0; font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 400\">Work backwards from the light</h2>\n\n\n\n<p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.75; color: #3A342F\">A twenty-minute ceremony that ends forty-five minutes before sunset leaves room for a receiving line, family photos in open shade, and ten quiet minutes with just the two of you while the light is at its best.</p>\n\n\n<p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.75; color: #3A342F\">If your ceremony faces west, ask the venue where the sun will sit at that hour. Guests squinting into it is the most common thing that goes wrong, and the easiest to fix by turning the chairs.</p>\n\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex: 0 0 280px; display: flex; flex-direction: column\">\n<div style=\"margin-bottom: 20px\"><div style=\"font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ECE8E2; margin-bottom: 12px\">Written by</div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 10px\"><div style=\"width: 64px; height: 64px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E9E5DF url(/template-photos/bride-window.webp) center / cover no-repeat; flex-shrink: 0\"></div><div style=\"font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 20px\">Maya Okonkwo</div></div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; color: #5A534C\">Bay Area wedding and portrait photographer.</div></div>\n<div style=\"margin-bottom: 20px\"><div style=\"font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ECE8E2; margin-bottom: 12px\">Related posts</div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px\"><div style=\"width: 64px; height: 64px; flex-shrink: 0; background: #E9E5DF url(/template-photos/golden-hour-ceremony.webp) center / cover no-repeat; border-radius: 4px\"></div><div style=\"font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.25\">A Shot List Your Photographer Will Actually Use</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px\"><div style=\"width: 64px; height: 64px; flex-shrink: 0; background: #E9E5DF url(/template-photos/venue-barn.webp) center / cover no-repeat; border-radius: 4px\"></div><div style=\"font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.25\">Small Oakland Venues That Feel Like a Dinner Party</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px\"><div style=\"width: 64px; height: 64px; flex-shrink: 0; background: #E9E5DF url(/template-photos/forest-sunbeams.webp) center / cover no-repeat; border-radius: 4px\"></div><div style=\"font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.25\">Ana &amp; Theo: A Rainy Day at the Redwood Grange</div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
